{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-353129",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "First, we find the values of $\\theta $ for which the two curves intersect:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ 4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  & =2 \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis gives us two solutions for $\\theta \\in [-\\pi ,\\pi ]:$\n\n$$\n\\theta =\\frac{\\pi }{6},\\frac{5\\pi }{6}\n$$\n\nTo determine which is the inner function and which is the outer, let's draw an arrow from the origin that passes through the shaded region.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14226762/assets/dd265c911aa4fc5713b0e53cea2ee751e84cd7c54b2b2aefb83bfae8d1f7d92f.png)\n\nThe arrow\n\n- *enters* the region through the inner function $r=2-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,$ and\n\n- *leaves* through the outer function $r=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta .$\n\nTo find the area, we use the formula\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}([\\text{outer}]^{2}-[\\text{inner}]^{2})\\,\\text{d}\\theta ,\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$\\,$ ${\\theta }_{1}=\\frac{\\pi }{6},\\,$ and $\\,{\\theta }_{2}=\\frac{5\\pi }{6}.$ \n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{5\\pi /6}((2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )^{2}-(2-2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )^{2})\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{5\\pi /6}(4{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta -(4-8\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +4{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta ))\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{5\\pi /6}(8\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -4)\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(-8\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -4\\theta )\\,{|}_{\\pi /6}^{5\\pi /6} \\\\  & =-2(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +\\theta )\\,{|}_{\\pi /6}^{5\\pi /6} \\\\  & =-2(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{5\\pi }{6})+\\frac{5\\pi }{6})+2(2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{6})+\\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =-2(-\\sqrt{3}+\\frac{5\\pi }{6})+2(\\sqrt{3}+\\frac{\\pi }{6}) \\\\  & =4\\sqrt{3}-\\frac{4\\pi }{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
